{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Data map — UCESCO Volunteer Manager{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
{{ include('datamap/_map_styles.html.twig') }}
{% verbatim %}
<style>
.datamap{
  color:var(--ink);font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;
  max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:56px;
}
.datamap *{box-sizing:border-box}
.datamap h1,.datamap h2,.datamap h3{line-height:1.15;text-wrap:balance;margin:0}
.datamap h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.datamap h2{font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3vw,1.9rem);font-weight:700}
.datamap h3{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700}
.datamap p{margin:0}
.datamap .prose{max-width:66ch;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
.datamap p.prose{display:block}
.datamap .eyebrow{font-weight:600;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--brand-ink)}
.datamap .lede{font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--muted)}
.datamap code,.datamap .tbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.82em;color:var(--muted)}
.datamap header{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
.datamap section{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:22px}


.datamap .detail{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px 32px;padding:22px;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;margin-top:16px}
.datamap .detail header{grid-column:1/-1;gap:4px}
.datamap .detail dl{margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
.datamap .detail dt{font-weight:700;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.2;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted)}
.datamap .detail dd{margin:4px 0 0}
.datamap .detail ul{margin:4px 0 0;padding-left:1.1em;list-style:disc}
@media (max-width:720px){.datamap .detail{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

.datamap .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}
.datamap .chip{font-weight:600;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}
.datamap .chip[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--brand);border-color:var(--brand);color:var(--paper)}
.datamap .chip:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--brand);outline-offset:2px}

.datamap .rules{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(290px,1fr));gap:16px}
.datamap .rule{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.datamap .rule .so{font-size:.93rem;color:var(--muted)}
.datamap .rule.key{border-color:var(--loop);background:var(--green-soft)}
.datamap .rule.key .so{color:var(--ink)}

.datamap .tablewrap{overflow-x:auto;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px}
.datamap table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:760px;font-size:.95rem}
.datamap th,.datamap td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:14px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.datamap tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}
.datamap th{font-weight:700;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.2;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted);background:var(--ground)}
.datamap td:first-child{font-weight:700;width:22%}
.datamap .plus{color:var(--green)} .datamap .minus{color:var(--warn)}
.datamap .rev{display:inline-block;font-weight:700;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1;padding:5px 9px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap}
.datamap .rev.easy{background:var(--green-soft);color:var(--green)}
.datamap .rev.mid{background:var(--warn-soft);color:var(--warn)}
.datamap .adr{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;margin-top:4px}

.datamap .questions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:16px}
.datamap .q{border-top:3px solid var(--brand);padding-top:14px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.datamap .q .eg{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}

.datamap .open{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:16px}
.datamap .card{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
.datamap .status{align-self:flex-start;font-weight:700;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1;padding:5px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--warn-soft);color:var(--warn)}
.datamap .opts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}
.datamap .opt{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font-size:.92rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
@media (max-width:480px){.datamap .opts{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

.datamap .backstage{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);border-left:3px solid var(--line);padding-left:16px;max-width:70ch}
.datamap footer{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px}
.datamap [hidden]{display:none!important}
</style>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{% verbatim %}
<div class="datamap wrap">

<header>
  <span class="eyebrow">Mikono · Volunteer Manager UCESCO</span>
  <h1>What the application keeps, and how it all fits together</h1>
  <p class="lede prose">Each box below is a <strong>list</strong> that the application keeps (it's called a “table”). Each arrow says that one record <strong>points to</strong> another. No need to read code: this map is for discussing what a change would break or make possible, before making it.</p>
</header>

<section aria-labelledby="h-carte">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="h-carte">The map</h2>
    <p>In the centre, the <strong>activity log</strong>: this is what the Volunteer Manager enters every day. On the left, the people. On the right, how the field work is organised. At the top, the branches, which connect the two sides.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Choose a list">
    <button class="chip" data-pick="activite" aria-pressed="true">Activity</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="volontaire" aria-pressed="false">Volunteer</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="sejour" aria-pressed="false">Stay</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="branche" aria-pressed="false">Branch</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="projet" aria-pressed="false">Project</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="programme" aria-pressed="false">Program</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="type" aria-pressed="false">Activity type</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="escorte" aria-pressed="false">Escort</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="user" aria-pressed="false">User</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="photo" aria-pressed="false">Photo</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="achievement" aria-pressed="false">Achievement</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="skill" aria-pressed="false">Skill</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="source" aria-pressed="false">Source</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="groupe" aria-pressed="false">Beneficiary group</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="indicator" aria-pressed="false">Indicator</button>
    <button class="chip" data-pick="none" aria-pressed="false">Show all</button>
  </div>

{% endverbatim %}
{{ include('datamap/_map.html.twig', {focusing: true}) }}
{% verbatim %}

  <article class="detail" id="detail" aria-live="polite"><header><span class="eyebrow">the log</span><h3 style="font-size:1.5rem">Activity</h3></header>
  <dl><div><dt>What it contains</dt><dd>What a volunteer did on a given day: the date, the duration (half day, full day, or other with details), notes, and who entered it.</dd></div><div><dt>Connected to</dt><dd><ul><li>1 volunteer</li><li>1 stay, found automatically from the date: never picked by hand</li><li>1 program, and therefore 1 project (derived)</li><li>1 activity type</li><li>0, 1 or several escorts</li><li>1 user (who entered it)</li></ul></dd></div></dl>
  <dl><div><dt>Rules</dt><dd><ul><li>Refused if no stay covers the date.</li><li>Refused if the project is not in the stay's branch.</li><li>Refused if the program does not offer this type or is not open that day.</li><li>In a batch: all or nothing.</li></ul></dd></div><div><dt>Deleting</dt><dd>Allowed. It is the only record that nothing else references.</dd></div></dl></article>
  <p class="hint">Click a box (or a button above) to see what it contains, what it connects to and what you are allowed to do with it.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-regles">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="h-regles">Six rules the application enforces</h2>
    <p>They are what makes the reports reliable. Any new idea must say which of them it affects.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3>1. One row = one volunteer, one day</h3><p class="so">A group of five volunteers sent to a site is five activities. Batch entry creates them in one go, and it is <strong>all or nothing</strong>: if a single volunteer causes a problem, nothing is saved.</p></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3>2. Status is not a checkbox</h3><p class="so">A volunteer is <strong>present</strong> when one of their stays covers today, <strong>upcoming</strong> when one starts later, <strong>past</strong> when all have ended, and has <strong>no stay</strong> otherwise. Nobody has to update it, and it cannot be wrong. The trade-off: <strong>no stay, no activity entry</strong>.</p></div>
    <div class="rule key"><h3>3. The branch loop must close</h3><p class="so">An activity's project, like an achievement's, must be in the same branch as the volunteer's stay on that day. A volunteer staying in Mombasa cannot be logged on a Kibera project. This is the green loop in the diagram.</p></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3>4. The program frames the task</h3><p class="so">The activity type must be one of those the program offers, and the date must fall within its dates (if it has any).</p></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3>5. What has been used is never deleted</h3><p class="so">A volunteer, project, program, type, escort, user, branch, skill, source, beneficiary group or indicator already referenced somewhere cannot be deleted: the button is greyed out. Projects, escorts, users and branches can be <strong>deactivated</strong> instead, and the history stays intact. Having added or edited a record does not count: such a user can be deleted, and the record loses its author.</p></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3>6. Dates are days in Nairobi</h3><p class="so">No hours, no time zones: an activity takes place on a calendar day, Kenya time, wherever the server is.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-choix">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="h-choix">Choices already made: what they brought, what they cost</h2>
    <p>Each row corresponds to a written decision (an “ADR”). If one of these costs becomes a problem in the field, that is the right time to raise it again.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>The choice</th><th>What it allows</th><th>What it costs</th><th>Going back on it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Several escorts per activity<span class="adr">ADR 0013</span></td><td class="plus">The WhatsApp attendance sheets are copied as they are; “By escort” tab in the reports.</td><td class="minus">We know <em>which days</em> an escort was present, not <em>for how long</em>. Knowing that would require entering it.</td><td><span class="rev mid">Model change</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Optional last name<span class="adr">ADR 0014</span></td><td class="plus">You enter “Daphne” right away, without blocking the entry.</td><td class="minus">Two “Ellen”s without a last name get mixed up in the pick lists.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Easy if the names are filled in</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Presence tied to dated stays<span class="adr">ADR 0026</span></td><td class="plus">The status (present, upcoming, past) is always right; we know which branch each volunteer was at, every day.</td><td class="minus">One more step: create the stay before the first activity. Two stays cannot overlap.</td><td><span class="rev mid">Affects the whole log</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Every project belongs to a branch<span class="adr">ADR 0027</span></td><td class="plus">Totals per branch possible; adding a country = adding a branch, with no development.</td><td class="minus">Moving a project to another branch is refused if it already has activities elsewhere.</td><td><span class="rev mid">Model change</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>A “Program” level between project and activity<span class="adr">ADR 0030</span></td><td class="plus">Offered types and opening dates are framed; totals per program in the reports.</td><td class="minus">A program is needed before anything can be entered on a new project. A program in use can no longer change project.</td><td><span class="rev mid">Affects the whole log</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Photo kept in the database<span class="adr">ADR 0032</span></td><td class="plus">Backed up automatically with everything else; never accessible without being signed in.</td><td class="minus">The database grows (about 100 KB per photo). Only one photo per volunteer.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Passport number encrypted<span class="adr">ADR 0033</span></td><td class="plus">A stolen database or backup does not reveal passport numbers.</td><td class="minus">Lose the key and every number is lost. The number can't be searched or exported.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skills as one shared list<span class="adr">ADR 0036</span></td><td class="plus">Volunteers and programs use the same words, so the Matches page can pair them.</td><td class="minus">A skill missing from the list must be added before anyone can pick it.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Recruitment sources as one shared list<span class="adr">ADR 0041</span></td><td class="plus">Volunteers can be counted per channel in the reports.</td><td class="minus">A new channel must be added to the list before anyone can pick it.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gender recorded, optionally<span class="adr">ADR 0037</span></td><td class="plus">Volunteers can be paired for shared accommodation.</td><td class="minus">Sensitive under Kenya's data protection law: profile page, the admin whole-database export and the admin API, which sends it to Anthropic; never in a list, report or list export.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Achievements recorded on a stay<span class="adr">ADR 0038</span></td><td class="plus">Each milestone is dated and placed at a project; its anniversary comes back on the home screen.</td><td class="minus">A stay is needed first, and deleting the stay deletes its achievements.</td><td><span class="rev mid">Model change</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sign-ins kept for 90 days<span class="adr">ADR 0028</span></td><td class="plus">Admins see failed attempts and the addresses that keep trying.</td><td class="minus">This is personal data (email + IP address), hence the limited duration and admin-only access.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Who added and last edited a record<span class="adr">ADR 0043</span></td><td class="plus">Each user's page lists the volunteers, stays, achievements, activities, projects and programs they added or last edited, and a volunteer's page says who added and last edited it.</td><td class="minus">Only the last editor is known, deletions are not recorded, and records from before 4 October 2026 have no author.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Admins can ask Claude or ChatGPT about the data<span class="adr">ADR 0050</span></td><td class="plus">Questions are answered from live records, with links back to the screens, and every read is listed on the Usage page for 90 days.</td><td class="minus">Volunteers' personal data, emergency contacts and gender included, goes to Anthropic or OpenAI outside Kenya. Passport numbers never do. Read-only, admins only.</td><td><span class="rev easy">Reversible</span></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-questions">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="h-questions">Four questions before adding a piece of information</h2>
    <p>A new request (“we'd also like to record…”) almost always comes down to these four questions. Their answers decide where it goes on the map, and therefore what it will cost.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="questions">
    <div class="q"><h3>What does it describe?</h3><p>The volunteer (once and for all) or what they did that day (on every activity)?</p><p class="eg">Profession goes on the volunteer. The number of children seen would go on the activity, and would be entered every day.</p></div>
    <div class="q"><h3>Required or optional?</h3><p>Required guarantees complete reports, but blocks entry when it isn't known.</p><p class="eg">That is why the last name became optional.</p></div>
    <div class="q"><h3>Fixed list or free text?</h3><p>A list can be counted and filtered in the reports. Free text can be read, but not counted.</p><p class="eg">Activity types and skills are lists; a volunteer's interests are free text.</p></div>
    <div class="q"><h3>Does it change over time?</h3><p>If so, and we want the history, it needs dates (“from… to…”), like stays.</p><p class="eg">Otherwise, the old value is overwritten and lost.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-ouvert">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="h-ouvert">Pending decisions</h2>
    <p>One item in the backlog directly affects the map.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="open">
    <div class="card">
      <span class="status">To decide</span>
      <h3>Attaching documents to volunteers</h3>
      <p>Passport, police clearance, signed agreement: up to about twenty files per volunteer, currently scattered across inboxes and WhatsApp. A new “Document” box attached to Volunteer, like the photo. What remains is choosing where to store the files.</p>
      <div class="opts">
        <div class="opt"><b>In the database</b><span class="plus">Backed up by default, like the photos.</span><span class="minus">The database grows fast (several MB per passport): heavier backups.</span></div>
        <div class="opt"><b>In a separate folder</b><span class="plus">Lightweight database.</span><span class="minus">A second thing to back up and restore, and not to forget.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">Either way: never accessible without signing in, deleted along with the volunteer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="h-coulisses">
  <h2 id="h-coulisses">Behind the scenes</h2>
  <p class="backstage">Two lists exist outside the map because they are not about volunteers: <strong>sign-in attempts</strong> (email typed, success, IP address, erased after 90 days) and anonymous <strong>usage gestures</strong> (“a roster was copied”), which feed the admin-only Usage screen. They are never mixed: one is personal, the other must not be.</p>
</section>

<footer>State of the model as of 4 October 2026. The “ADR” references point to the decisions written up in <code>docs/adr/</code> in the Mikono repository.</footer>

